              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сенсация (sensátsiya) — \"a sensation\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Эта новость стала настоящей сенсацией. Éta nóvost stála nastoyáshchey sensátsiyey. This news became a real sensation."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. The adjective is сенсационный."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сенсация (sensátsiya) was borrowed from French sensation, built on Latin sensus \"feeling\", from sentīre \"to feel\" (Lewis & Short); EtymDB lists the Russian word with no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
